   "nvidia_t4g": [
    "b69f0d18b2a40708e697f569e610d34e66ae66d520225da4446d9e959f4a618e  /home/ubuntu/capture-hw/bin/hw_capture",
    "== yuv420p",
    "[Vulkan @ 0xb3a7cb81d2a0] Device 0 selected: NVIDIA T4G (discrete) (0x1eb4)",
    "[swscaler @ 0xb3a7ccfe1a10] Failed initializing scaling graph (Operation not supported): fmt:rgba csp:gbr prim:unknown trc:unknown -> fmt:yuv420p csp:bt470bg prim:unknown trc:unknown",
    "hw_capture: buffersink get",
    "== nv12",
    "[Vulkan @ 0xbe92e9a072a0] Device 0 selected: NVIDIA T4G (discrete) (0x1eb4)",
    "[swscaler @ 0xbe92eb1cb830] Failed initializing scaling graph (Operation not supported): fmt:rgba csp:gbr prim:unknown trc:unknown -> fmt:nv12 csp:bt470bg prim:unknown trc:unknown",
    "hw_capture: buffersink get",
    "== yuv444p",
    "[Vulkan @ 0xae5c0f9212a0] Device 0 selected: NVIDIA T4G (discrete) (0x1eb4)",
    "[swscaler @ 0xae5c110e58c0] Failed initializing scaling graph (Operation not supported): fmt:rgba csp:gbr prim:unknown trc:unknown -> fmt:yuv444p csp:bt470bg prim:unknown trc:unknown",
    "hw_capture: buffersink get"
   ],
   "verdict": "swscale's Vulkan ops backend (used by scale_vulkan at equal size) has no 4:2:0 subsampling: yuv420p and nv12 fail with ENOTSUP on both devices; yuv444p compiles on MoltenVK only"
  },
  "scale_vulkan_on_nvidia_t4g": "the SPIR-V backend fails even for yuv444p: 'No memory type found for flags 0x3' (it asks for DEVICE_LOCAL|HOST_VISIBLE memory for a buffer whose memoryTypeBits exclude the T4G's only such type), so FFmpeg 9.0.2 has no working scale_vulkan conversion on this GPU",
  "scale_cuda": "scale_cuda in 9.0.2 has no RGB-input to YUV-output kernels (format table in libavfilter/vf_scale_cuda.c, inspected on the pinned source); not usable for the contract",
  "scale_vt": "scale_vt (VideoToolbox) in 9.0.2 resizes VideoToolbox surfaces but cannot convert pixel formats (source inspection during this evaluation); not usable for RGBA -> YUV 4:2:0",
  "libplacebo": "vf_libplacebo (libplacebo v7.351.0) converts RGBA -> YUV 4:2:0 entirely on the GPU on both devices; it always holds one frame back (pl_queue needs the next frame), declares alpha-composited input unless the input is RGB0, and its chroma downsampling differs from swscale's (see platform results)",
  "upstream_observations": [
   "vflip_vulkan (libavfilter/vulkan/flip.comp.glsl) writes row size.y - pos.y instead of size.y - 1 - pos.y: the output is shifted one row and row 0 is never written",
   "libavfilter/vulkan/Makefile builds flip.comp.spv.o only under CONFIG_FLIP_VULKAN_FILTER, so enabling vflip_vulkan alone fails to link",
   "hwupload of a frame with a negative linesize (swscale's bottom-up idiom) segfaults on MoltenVK (eval-mac-v1, cases c09/c07)",
   "libplacebo v7.351.0's vk.xml generator fails under Python 3.15's ElementTree (TypeError: expected an Element, not ElementTree); built with Python 3.12"
  ]
 },
